ntion of VBAT anywhere in the specification's power section.\"}], \"impact\": \"A floating VBAT pin can leave the RTC/backup domain unpowered or in an undefined state and may cause unreliable behaviour, although the main functions may still run.\", \"confidence\": 0.2}], \"summary\": \"The schematic is largely consistent with the specification: the NFC and display buses, the SWD header, the TSC wiring and the decoupling all match. The most likely deviation is the OLED interface-select strapping on BS0/BS1, which as drawn does not match the specified I2C mode, and the floating VBAT pin is a secondary concern.\"}",
